<title>SWITZERLAND: Australian Nobel laureate Eccles dead at 94.</title>
<headline>Australian Nobel laureate Eccles dead at 94.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian neurophysiologist and Nobel Prize winner Sir John Eccles died at Locarno Hospital on Friday after a long illness at the age of 94, hospital officials said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Eccles, won the Nobel Prize for medicine in 1963, had lived in the Locarno area for some 25 years.</p>
<p>His work had a great influence on the medical treatment of nervous disease.</p>
</text>
